# Preferred agent skills

Always start domain/module work with the repo skill:

- `.cursor/skills/futrob-hexagonal-module/SKILL.md`

Cloud Agents only auto-load skills committed under `.cursor/skills/` (and `.agents/skills/`).
User-level `~/.cursor/skills` / `~/.agents/skills` and personal plugins do not sync to the VM.
When a listed skill file is missing, follow the matching `.cursor/rules` and `AGENTS.md` instead
of inventing a parallel stack.

## Domain and product thinking

Read and follow these when the task matches.

| Skill | When |
|---|---|
| **futrob-hexagonal-module** | Any BC, use case, port, adapter, or server function |
| **futrob-cli** | Smoke-testing domain use cases or `apps/api` endpoints via `apps/cli` (incl. `e2e-golden-path`); adding CLI commands |
| **layers-domain** | Clarify or rename domain concepts before coding (Encounter, OfficialMatch, Team, selection) |
| **layers-interaction-flow** | Captain selection, reschedule, sync → review → officialize flows before UI/API shape |
| **layers-user-needs** | Operator vs spectator jobs, pains, and opportunities before solution shape |
| **layers-surface** | Audit screens against vocabulary, completeness, feedback, and hierarchy |

## UI system

Compose from `@futrob/ui`. Do not invent a second visual language.

| Skill | When |
|---|---|
| **shadcn** (Vercel plugin / CLI) | Add or change primitives in `packages/ui`; compose in web presentation. Base UI only — see `ui-shadcn.mdc` |
| **better-ui** | Visual pass: density, polish, empty/error states, operator vs spectator UI |
| **better-layout** | Grouping, spacing, reading order, breakpoints, progressive disclosure |
| **better-typography** | Type roles, wrapping, tabular numbers, measure — keep Manrope + `typo-*` |
| **better-accessibility** | Focus, keyboard, names, 44 px targets, reduced motion |
| **better-colors** | Contrast and semantic tokens only; do not invent new primitive colors |
| **better-writing** | Labels, errors, empty copy; Spanish/English; `typo-caption` is sentence case |
| **design-empty-states** | First-use, filtered-empty, permission, and recoverable-error panels |
| **smooth-shadow-ring** | Elevated surfaces. Never pair `border`/`ring` with `shadow` |
| **gsap** (gsap-skills plugin) | Landing / bracket zoom/pan presence, intentional transitions. Never in domain/application. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` |

## App and platform

| Skill | When |
|---|---|
| **tanstack-start** | Routes, SSR loaders, server functions, Workers entry — see `tanstack-start.mdc` |
| **tanstack-query** | Client `/api/v1` server-state (`useQuery` / `useMutation`). See ADR-0012 |
| **web-perf** | SSR/Workers budgets, dense lists, bracket, public portal load |
| **seo** | Public landing and competition portal metadata; crawlable published content only |
| **wrangler** | D1, R2, Queues, Cron, secrets, `wrangler.jsonc` |
| **workers-best-practices** | Workers runtime, bindings, streaming, no Node assumptions at module scope |
| **sentry-instrument** | Sentry at execution boundaries (server functions, queue/cron, API) |
| **typescript-best-practices** (pstack) | Contracts, discriminated unions, branded IDs, exhaustive switches |

## Local tooling

- `apps/cli` is the domain/use-case playground (fakes in memory) and API smoke tool. See `/apps/cli/README.md` and the `futrob-cli` skill above.
- Product deployable remains `apps/web` only.

## Do not use for implementation here

Supabase, Railway deploy of `apps/web`, Clerk, Convex, Nuxt, Astro, UnoCSS, Kapso/Chat SDK,
industrial-brutalist-ui, stitch-design-taste, or Next.js — unless product direction explicitly
reopens them. `apps/api` already runs on Railway; do not move the Must web deployable there.
